# ERP Domain Rules

## Tenancy

- Every merchant-owned record has `tenantId`
- API guards enforce tenant scope from JWT `tenantId` claim
- Platform cross-tenant access requires `@BypassTenant()` + audit log
- Never return another tenant's data, even on 404 (use generic "not found")

## Merchant Onboarding

States: `DRAFT` → `SUBMITTED` → `UNDER_REVIEW` → `APPROVED` | `REJECTED`

- Login blocked until `APPROVED`
- Approval provisions Tenant slug, activates owner User
- Rejection stores `rejectionReason`, notifies via BullMQ

## CRM

- Pipeline stages: `NEW` → `QUALIFIED` → `WON` | `LOST`
- Activities: `CALL`, `NOTE`, `MEETING` — always linked to contact or lead
- QR bind auto-creates lead with `source: DISTRIBUTOR_QR`

## Distributors

- `commissionType`: `PERCENT` (0-100) or `FIXED` (currency units)
- `commissionRate` stored as Decimal(10,4)
- Settlement calculation is Phase 2 — Phase 1 stores settings only

## QR Binding

- Token: HMAC-signed JWT with `distributorId`, `tenantId`, `bindType`, `exp`
- Default expiry: 7 days
- One active binding per merchant (`@@unique([bindableType, bindableId])`)
- Bind URL: `{MERCHANT_APP_URL}/bind/{token}`

## Auth Realms

| aud | Portal | Roles |
|-----|--------|-------|
| `admin` | apps/admin | SUPER_ADMIN, PLATFORM_OPS |
| `merchant` | apps/merchant | MERCHANT_OWNER, MERCHANT_STAFF |
| `store` | apps/store | CUSTOMER (Phase 2) |

Separate cookie namespaces per portal. Never mix JWT audiences.

## Shared Types

All enums and DTOs in `packages/shared`. Import in API and all frontends.
